{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2332 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "2fa83135beba81421c47bcd99f6c7a6b736b6ed7883979d932bc9e123097d82d" :edb/db-before-t 2331 :edb/db-after-t 2332 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535644 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:21:51.484Z" 13194139535644 true] [17592186124391 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359034 13194139535644 true] [17592186124391 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359048 13194139535644 true] [17592186124392 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359041 13194139535644 true] [17592186124392 1020 #edb/ref 17592186359055 13194139535644 true] [17592186124867 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535644 true] [17592186124867 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible? \n\n- $x\\in [-4,0]$\n- $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,1)$" 13194139535644 true] [17592186124867 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1889/Source/Images/q-36039.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n1. $x ∈ [- 4, 0]$\n2. $[MATH: x ∈ (-4,-2]]$\n3. $x ∈ (-3, 1)$" 13194139535644 false] [17592186124867 1145 "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139535644 true] [17592186359034 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359035 13194139535644 true] [17592186359034 1089 "q-108667" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359034 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535644 true] [17592186359034 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/811ead4928d2f245235736dce473d121261ea358ca4ff3a0cc8b01bb2e9f3b31.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-3,3)$\n- $x\\in [1,4]$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3]$" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359034 1113 #uuid "07ce3cd4-47b8-5b1e-860e-1b9099cab604" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359034 1145 "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/32f1ad5bdec30951900a1c30c2996ea040e65880f859c43769faf374db06a2f0.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,3)$ and $x\\in [1,4]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/8ed451b24fa83de513f4a1b5c79d39f94add784c6b7265e765a3381e7b03363a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359036 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359037 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359038 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359039 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359040 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1041 "selection" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359038 13194139535644 true] [17592186359035 1110 #uuid "78364d24-42eb-5b28-87c1-77b4f2b27aa0" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359036 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359036 1111 #uuid "46fa9d60-f6f5-5b63-86a4-2449214ab6cd" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359037 1034 "I only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359037 1111 #uuid "f0f25d39-db78-5394-b4d0-bc5544af92d3" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359038 1034 "III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359038 1111 #uuid "1882bd91-c950-586a-a609-ab5ec7e41b2f" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359039 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359039 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359039 1111 #uuid "cc2498d4-c5e6-594e-9bc2-7feb3530daa2" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359040 1034 "II only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359040 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359040 1111 #uuid "0e5e97c8-b041-516c-96ca-9b38b7ff41f5" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359041 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359042 13194139535644 true] [17592186359041 1089 "q-36010" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359041 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535644 true] [17592186359041 1100 "Given that $f(x)=|x-2|+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (2,4]$" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359041 1113 #uuid "a802d1bc-5bd8-512e-a33b-811eae18f7fb" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359041 1145 "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-2|+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-2|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-2|$ by $1$ unit up to get $f(x)=|x-2|+1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/ceab1637313ae53869cc1e59f6a56ad6cb920a83dffba482558b696188df0d36.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (2,4].$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a47169838785b6f4ac78253252bcedc3c2cb752a655feac9945e20dd40563b4f.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/14ed35294e1179ffd9efaf87fa8ac1eb99853a7da344e462c2cb0dda74c3b78f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359043 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359044 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359045 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359046 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359047 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1041 "selection" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359044 13194139535644 true] [17592186359042 1110 #uuid "9861c43d-6fd9-56b1-9cb4-217ce804b08f" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359043 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359043 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359043 1111 #uuid "5c0f6b3e-77a4-5114-9a8a-e1f304a8ce44" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359044 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359044 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359044 1111 #uuid "26837314-0271-5c4e-a74f-980999b80d50" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359045 1034 "I only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359045 1111 #uuid "627dfaec-dd9e-555c-9a00-1edccd5d30af" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359046 1034 "III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359046 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359046 1111 #uuid "1fecb6c3-e227-5b30-a1d2-5b8b2fdcc4b9" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359047 1034 "II only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359047 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359047 1111 #uuid "480e0767-db4a-5fd3-9260-40855d6eef7e" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359048 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359049 13194139535644 true] [17592186359048 1089 "q-36934" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359048 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535644 true] [17592186359048 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/1eccd6630b69558f8a86f8336e9f0e49f37ffb29acf4a3c8f58be34346b4c93c.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $x\\in [-2,0]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-2]$\n- $x\\in (-3,-1]$" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359048 1113 #uuid "75b2a4c0-9fd0-5022-a065-c7880b09f9c0" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359048 1145 "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-2,0]$  and $x\\in (-3,-1]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/d8cc826df6fed7a4106539d88ffa8a1fdc0529904497c2d5413f9761acaccd12.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/bc00ed8f4bdf03b248dbd9a1651ed073e352d512b830139505fba3b60e05e7e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only\"." 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359050 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359051 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359052 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359053 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359054 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1041 "selection" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359054 13194139535644 true] [17592186359049 1110 #uuid "144991a2-b665-55e4-814e-32353a9eec94" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359050 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359050 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359050 1111 #uuid "25309cc9-0c6a-54d8-8dfb-0fc2b32a6981" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359051 1034 "III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359051 1111 #uuid "21499e87-a101-51de-9889-40e1414131a0" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359052 1034 "None" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359052 1111 #uuid "26a3be6d-a0f3-5e45-a2ea-e5f2626892d6" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359053 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359053 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359053 1111 #uuid "7425990f-cecb-5f41-99b8-18f12baefd75" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359054 1034 "II  only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359054 1111 #uuid "2e8f9e8c-9047-5a6a-a566-7c628516655b" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359055 1017 #edb/ref 17592186359056 13194139535644 true] [17592186359055 1089 "q-66729" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359055 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535644 true] [17592186359055 1100 "Given that $f(x)=|x-1|-2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359055 1113 #uuid "d0455465-8a85-5aa8-911c-68ab12f14b4d" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359055 1145 "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-1|-2$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-1|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-1|$ by $2$ units down to get $f(x)=|x-1|-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/753840da17642582f9dbc0debc18f1fa3efcbbb11142894c1dd823ad6c0c630a.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/15f1c797cbddd2ac8e2e9c5be72f842e7d1accfc5f619af57b1f35a27e1015c0.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068486/assets/a100489b49da7b06c98783b1b1c4ec0de9d891fc2b22f4b36b1a0ac2d54fc4f3.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"." 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359057 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359058 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359059 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359060 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1000 #edb/ref 17592186359061 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1041 "selection" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1104 #edb/ref 17592186359061 13194139535644 true] [17592186359056 1110 #uuid "7b3cb55c-3394-58c9-8fc9-5e66544e30a2" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359057 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359057 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359057 1111 #uuid "bd3a0213-e6fb-54df-8107-ee0148cf080c" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359058 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359058 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359058 1111 #uuid "a0f0c6c9-a3f0-5632-adc2-4914b9bb05a8" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359059 1034 "I only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359059 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359059 1111 #uuid "7766579a-d19d-52c0-a069-ba07a3f86eed" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359060 1034 "III only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359060 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359060 1111 #uuid "e0867068-bc55-5ee9-898b-5c341a66317c" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359061 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535644 true] [17592186359061 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535644 true] [17592186359061 1111 #uuid "1e4e615b-b8bd-5d55-a45c-968620500c37" 13194139535644 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-108667" 17592186359034 "q-108667/selection" 17592186359035 "q-108667/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f7969